React TypeScript Firebase PartyKit Connect4
You are an expert in TypeScript, React, Firebase Authentication, PartyKit multiplayer, and Tailwind CSS.

Key Principles
- Write clean, maintainable TypeScript code with proper type definitions.
- Use functional components and custom hooks for code organization.
- Separate game logic from UI components.
- Implement real-time multiplayer features using PartyKit's room-based architecture.
- Handle authentication and user management through Firebase.

Project Structure
/src
- components/: React UI components
- hooks/: Custom React hooks
- firebase/: Firebase configuration and utilities
- game/: Game logic and state management
- types/: TypeScript type definitions
- utils/: Helper functions and utilities
- assets/: Static assets and resources

Naming Conventions
- Use PascalCase for component files (GameBoard.tsx)
- Prefix hooks with "use" (useGameState.ts)
- Use camelCase for utility functions (calculateWinner.ts)
- Suffix type files with ".types.ts" (Game.types.ts)

TypeScript Usage
- Define interfaces for game state and player types
- Use strict TypeScript checking
- Avoid any types; use proper type definitions
- Leverage TypeScript for game move validation

Game Architecture
- Separate core game logic from UI components
- Use custom hooks for game state management
- Implement pure functions for game calculations
- Handle multiplayer synchronization through PartyKit

Firebase Integration
- Use Firebase Auth hooks for authentication state
- Implement proper security rules
- Handle user sessions and persistence
- Keep Firebase configuration centralized

PartyKit Implementation
- Use room-based architecture for game sessions
- Implement proper connection state handling
- Handle reconnection scenarios gracefully
- Sync game state across players efficiently

Performance Optimization
- Minimize unnecessary re-renders
- Use React.memo for heavy components
- Implement proper loading states
- Handle network latency gracefully

Error Handling
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Handle network disconnections
- Provide user feedback for game state
- Log errors appropriately (avoid console.log in production)

Testing
- Write unit tests for game logic
- Test multiplayer scenarios
- Verify authentication flows
- Test edge cases in game rules

Follow Firebase and PartyKit documentation for best practices in authentication and real-time multiplayer implementation.